</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
(<a href="#S5.F7.sf1" title="In Figure 7 ‣ 5.6 Efficiency Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a>) The prefilling time of MLA (full attention), hybrid GDN-H and our Kimi Linear.
(<a href="#S5.F7.sf2" title="In Figure 7 ‣ 5.6 Efficiency Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a>) The time per output token (TPOT) for MLA, GDN-H and Kimi Linear during decoding. (We use batch size = 1 here for tests.)
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prefilling &amp; Decoding speed</h5>

<div id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare the training and decoding times for full attention MLA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, GDN-H, and Kimi Linear in Figure <a href="#S5.F7.sf1" title="In Figure 7 ‣ 5.6 Efficiency Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S5.F7.sf2" title="In Figure 7 ‣ 5.6 Efficiency Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a>. Note that all models are based on the Kimi Linear 48B setting, with the same number of layers and attention heads.
We observe that:
1) Despite incorporating a more fine-grained decay mechanism, Kimi Linear introduces negligible latency overhead compared to GDN-H during prefilling.
As shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F7.sf1" title="In Figure 7 ‣ 5.6 Efficiency Comparison ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(a)</span></a>, their performance curves are virtually indistinguishable, confirming that our method maintains high efficiency.
The hybrid Kimi Linear model demonstrates a clear efficiency advantage over the MLA baseline as sequence length increases.
While its performance is comparable to MLA at shorter lengths (4k–16k), it becomes significantly faster from 128k onwards.
This efficiency gap widens dramatically at scale, with Kimi Linear outperforming MLA by a factor of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.3</annotation></semantics></math> for 512k sequences and <math id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.9</annotation></semantics></math> for 1M sequences.
As shown in Figure <a href="#S0.F1.sf2" title="In Figure 1 ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a>, Kimi Linear fully demonstrates its advantages during the decoding phase. For decoding at 1M context length, Kimi Linear is <math id="S5.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\times</annotation></semantics></math> faster than full attention.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussions</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Kimi Delta Attention as learnable position embeddings</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard attention in transformers is by design agnostic to the sequence order of its inputs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx99" title="" class="ltx_ref">99</a>]</cite>, thus necessitating explicit positional encodings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx75" title="" class="ltx_ref">75</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx86" title="" class="ltx_ref">86</a>]</cite>.
Among various methods, RoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx88" title="" class="ltx_ref">88</a>]</cite> has emerged as the <span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">de facto</span> standard in modern LLMs due to its effectiveness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx98" title="" class="ltx_ref">98</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
The mechanism of multiplicative positional encodings like RoPE can be analyzed through a generalized attention formulation:</p>
<table id="S6.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t,i}=\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\left(\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}\mathbf{R}_{j}\right)\bm{k}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t,i}=\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\left(\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}\mathbf{R}_{j}\right)\bm{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where the position relationship between the <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th query <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th key <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is reflected by the cumulative matrix products. RoPE defines the transformation matrix <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as a block diagonal matrix composed of <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}/2</annotation></semantics></math> 2D rotation matrices <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{j}^{k}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos(j\theta_{k})&amp;-\sin(j\theta_{k})\\
\sin(j\theta_{k})&amp;\cos(j\theta_{k})\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{j}^{k}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos(j\theta_{k})&amp;-\sin(j\theta_{k})\\
\sin(j\theta_{k})&amp;\cos(j\theta_{k})\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> with <span id="S6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">per-2-dimensional</span> angular frequency <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to the properties of rotation matrices, i.e., <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{t-i}=\mathbf{R}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{R}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{t-i}=\mathbf{R}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{R}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, absolute positional information <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be applied separately to <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are then transformed into relative positional information <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-i</annotation></semantics></math> encoded as <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}\mathbf{R}_{j}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos((t-i)\theta_{k})&amp;-\sin((t-i)\theta_{k})\\
\sin((t-i)\theta_{k})&amp;\cos((t-i)\theta_{k})\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}\mathbf{R}_{j}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos((t-i)\theta_{k})&amp;-\sin((t-i)\theta_{k})\\
\sin((t-i)\theta_{k})&amp;\cos((t-i)\theta_{k})\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, we show that linear attentions with the gated delta rule can be expressed in a comparable formulation in Eq. <a href="#S6.E12" title="In 6.1 Kimi Delta Attention as learnable position embeddings ‣ 6 Discussions ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
Similar forms for other attention variants are summarized in Table <a href="#S6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 6.1 Kimi Delta Attention as learnable position embeddings ‣ 6 Discussions ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
<table id="S6.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{o}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\left(\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{A}_{j}}\left(\mathbf{I}-\beta_{j}\bm{k}_{j}\bm{k}_{j}^{\top}\right)\right)\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝐀</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{o}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\left(\prod_{j=i+1}^{t}{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{A}_{j}}\left(\mathbf{I}-\beta_{j}\bm{k}_{j}\bm{k}_{j}^{\top}\right)\right)\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>
An overview of attention mechanisms in their mathematically equivalent recurrent (<math id="S6.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{o}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{o}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) and parallel (<math id="S6.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{O}</annotation></semantics></math>) forms.
We omitted the normalization term and <math id="S6.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to achieve a more concise representation.
The function <math id="S6.T6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the infinite-dimensional feature space corresponding to the exponential kernel, i.e., <math id="S6.T6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\bm{q})^{\top}\phi(\bm{k})=\exp(\bm{q}^{\top}\bm{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒌</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\bm{q})^{\top}\phi(\bm{k})=\exp(\bm{q}^{\top}\bm{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
<div id="S6.T6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:650.9pt;height:331.8pt;vertical-align:-163.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="S6.T6.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">

<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">Recurrent form</span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">Parallel form</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;">SA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx99" title="" class="ltx_ref">99</a>]</cite></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\exp\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\exp\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\exp\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\right)\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\exp\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\right)\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;">SA + RoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx88" title="" class="ltx_ref">88</a>]</cite></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\exp\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\bm{R}_{s}\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\exp\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\bm{R}_{s}\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\exp\left(\mathbf{R\left(Q\right)R\left(K\right)^{\top}}\right)\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\exp\left(\mathbf{R\left(Q\right)R\left(K\right)^{\top}}\right)\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;">LA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx101" title="" class="ltx_ref">101</a>]</cite></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
