<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\left({\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\alpha_{s}}-\bm{k}_{s}\bm{k}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\left({\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\alpha_{s}}-\bm{k}_{s}\bm{k}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathcal{A}}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\mathbf{KK^{\top}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathcal{A}^{i-1/j}}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#B92622">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐊𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#B92622">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mathbf{QK^{\top}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathcal{A}}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\mathbf{KK^{\top}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathcal{A}^{i-1/j}}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;">RWKV7 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx71" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\left({\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\operatorname{Diag}\left(\bm{\alpha}_{s}\right)}-\left(\bm{b}_{s}\odot\hat{\bm{k}}_{s}\right)\hat{\bm{k}}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝜶</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">s</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}\left({\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\operatorname{Diag}\left(\bm{\alpha}_{s}\right)}-\left(\bm{b}_{s}\odot\hat{\bm{k}}_{s}\right)\hat{\bm{k}}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\left(\mathbf{Q}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{{\mathbf{K}}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\left(\hat{\mathbf{K}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\overset{0\to t-1}{\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)\left(\frac{\tilde{\mathbf{K}}\odot\mathbf{B}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>𝐊</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622" mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622" mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622" mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622" mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622" mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow></mrow></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\left(\mathbf{Q}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{{\mathbf{K}}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\left(\hat{\mathbf{K}}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\overset{0\to t-1}{\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)\left(\frac{\tilde{\mathbf{K}}\odot\mathbf{B}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">KDA<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (ours)</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m35" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\operatorname{Diag}\left(\bm{\alpha}_{s}\right)}\left(\mathbf{I}-\bm{k}_{s}\bm{k}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" lspace="0em" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝒒</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" lspace="0em" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">t</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">𝜶</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">s</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐈</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝒌</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝒌</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝒌</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{j=1}^{t}\left(\bm{q}_{t}^{\top}{\left(\prod\limits_{s=j+1}^{t}{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\operatorname{Diag}\left(\bm{\alpha}_{s}\right)}\left(\mathbf{I}-\bm{k}_{s}\bm{k}_{s}^{\top}\right)\right)}\bm{k}_{j}\right)\bm{v}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S6.T6.2.1.1.1.14.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:2pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S6.T6.m36" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="\left(\left(\mathbf{Q}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{\mathbf{K}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\left(\mathbf{K}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{\mathbf{K}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐐</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" lspace="0.222em" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mfrac><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐊</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐌</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐈</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐊</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" lspace="0.222em" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">(</mo><mfrac><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐊</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B92622;--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathcolor="#B92622">𝚪</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐌</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\left(\mathbf{Q}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{\mathbf{K}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}\right)\left(\mathbf{I}+\left(\mathbf{K}\odot{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}\right)\left(\frac{\mathbf{K}}{{\color[rgb]{0.7266,0.1484,0.1328}\mathbf{\Gamma}}}\right)^{\top}\odot\mathbf{M}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></p>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">From this perspective, GDN can be interpreted as a form of multiplicative positional encoding whose transition matrix is data-dependent, thereby relaxing the orthogonality constraint imposed by RoPE and can be potentially more powerful <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx115" title="" class="ltx_ref">115</a>]</cite>.
<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
              
              
              
            When preserving orthogonality, absolute positional encodings can be applied independently to <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are then automatically transformed into relative positional encodings during the attention computation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx87" title="" class="ltx_ref">87</a>]</cite>.
</span></span></span>
This provides a potential solution to the known extrapolation issues of RoPE, whose fixed frequencies can cause overfitting to context lengths seen during training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx108" title="" class="ltx_ref">108</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite>.
Some recent works adopt workarounds like partial RoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> or even forgo explicit positional encodings entirely (NoPE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx76" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
Given that GDN serves as an analogue role to RoPE, we choose NoPE for global full attention layers (MLA) in our model, allowing positional information to be captured dynamically by our proposed KDA model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, a key strength of RoPE is its fine-grained positional encoding, achieved by assigning different rotation frequencies to each pair of dimensions, which functions analogously to a Nonuniform Fourier Transform <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bibx41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> along the feature dimension.
Standard GDN, however, employs a per-head scalar decay and lacks this per-dimensional diversity, which motivates us to propose KDA with a learnable channel-wise gate.</p>
</div>
