<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Kimi Linear@5.7T results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following Moonlight, we also trained Kimi Linear with an extended 5.7T token dataset to demonstrate its effectiveness. With <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity and a new attention architecture design, Kimi Linear consistently outperforms Moonlight across nearly all benchmarks, underscoring the efficacy of the new architecture. The results are shown in Table <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix D Kimi Linear@5.7T results ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for base model and Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix D Kimi Linear@5.7T results ‣ Kimi Linear:An Expressive, Efficient Attention Architecture" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> for instruction tuned model.
Moonlight-Instruct was not evaluated (“-”) on tasks exceeding its 8K context limit.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Kimi Linear@5.7T obtains a score of 94.8 on RULER at 1M context length. This long context performance reinforces that Kimi Linear is a promising alternative to full-attention architectures, delivering comparable or superior results while potentially offering more efficient resource utilization.</p>
</div>
